CUE's struct shorthand on a version file's top-level fields: Schema is
written with its braces, and a lens block with the braces after its
parameter, ForwardLens: (prev): {...}. Beneath them the shorthand is accepted
and Format expands it (see shorthand-inside).
-- ship/history/0.0.thema --
Schema: meta: {
	owner: string
}
-- ship/history/1.0.thema --
Schema: {
	meta: {
		owner: string
		team:  string
	}
}

ForwardLens: (prev): self: {
	meta: {
		team: "unassigned"
	}
}
-- ship/tip.thema --
Schema: {
	meta: {
		owner: string
		team:  string
	}
}
-- out/error --
error[E0109]: Schema: meta: ... is CUE's struct shorthand, which a version file's Schema does not use
 --> history/0.0.thema:1:9
  |
1 | Schema: meta: {
  |         ^^^^
  |
  = note: a version file's three fields keep their braces, so that each reads as the block it is
  = help: write Schema: {meta: ...}

error[E0109]: ForwardLens: (prev): self: ... is CUE's struct shorthand, which a version file's ForwardLens does not use
 --> history/1.0.thema:8:22
  |
8 | ForwardLens: (prev): self: {
  |                      ^^^^
  |
  = note: a lens keeps the braces after its parameter, so that it reads as a function of it
  = help: write ForwardLens: (prev): {self: ...}
